==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zroco]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~70 seconds<sup>800f~2,100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Zir Zeal]] spawns.
**1 [[Zigge]] spawns.
**1 [[Zomboe]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Possibly the most difficult stage in the sub-chapter. Build up as large of a ranged stack as possible to deal with the [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]]. [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] can be a big assistance in building a wallet against the Zrocos and B.B.Bunnies without having to start building a stack of ranged attackers. Teacher Bun Bun has a very large health pool, but against a stack of [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cats]], along with many other ranged attackers, he won't last long. Bringing [[:Category:Area Attack Enemies|Area Attackers]] is highly recommended to get rid of the Zir Zeal and Zigge. Beware of the Zrocos burrowing into your attackers because of their high damage and weaken ability.
Something that may help is stalling at the beginning until the Zomboes come out to minimize the number of zombies that appear alongside the Bun Bun. It is also recommended to bring [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] to help crowd control and deal damage to Bun Bun, respectively. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] is a great choice here, for obvious reasons.

==Trivia==
*Revenant Road may be a reference to [[wikipedia:Corpse road|corpse roads]], ancient paths that were used to transport corpses to churchyards for burial and had many superstitions and myths pertaining to the spirits of the dead.
*Revenant Road's Japanese name (ポルターガイストリート ''Porutāgaisutorīto'', "Poltergei St." or "Poltergeistreet"), is a combination of ''poltergeist'' and ''street'' and may be a reference to the movie ''[[wikipedia:Poltergeist (1982 film)|Poltergeist]]''.

